name: Bug report
description: Something doesn't work as expected, or results from a new or untested model.
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        Thanks for reporting. A diagnostics download answers most questions. It's designed
        to leave out private details, but look it over before posting anyway. Report security issues
        privately, as described in SECURITY.md, not here.
  - type: checkboxes
    id: new_model
    attributes:
      label: Model
      options:
        - label: This is a new or untested model (see the reporting guide in CONTRIBUTING.md)
  - type: textarea
    id: what
    attributes:
      label: What happened, and what did you expect?
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: input
    id: when
    attributes:
      label: When did it happen? (date, time, and time zone)
  - type: input
    id: model
    attributes:
      label: {{ device | capitalize }} model and firmware (on the device page)
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: input
    id: integration_version
    attributes:
      label: Integration version
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: input
    id: ha_version
    attributes:
      label: Home Assistant version
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: textarea
    id: diagnostics
    attributes:
      label: Diagnostics
      description: Device page > three dots menu > Download diagnostics. Drag the file here.
  - type: textarea
    id: log
    attributes:
      label: Debug log, if asked
      description: Integration page > three dots menu > Enable debug logging, make it happen again, then disable it to download the log.
  - type: textarea
    id: more
    attributes:
      label: Anything else
  - type: checkboxes
    id: privacy
    attributes:
      label: Privacy
      options:
        - label: I've looked over what I'm posting and removed anything I don't want public.
          required: true
